<ContentPage
  title="Privacy Policy | RentVsBuyMath"
  description="How RentVsBuyMath.com handles your data: calculations run in your browser, we collect no personal information, and we use privacy-respecting analytics."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="July 18, 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    Your financial inputs never leave your device. Every calculation on this site runs locally in
    your browser — nothing you type into the calculator is transmitted to us or stored on any
    server. There are no accounts, and we never ask for your name, email, income, or any other
    personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do collect</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, we use analytics to understand aggregate usage — which pages are visited,
    roughly where visitors come from, and how the site performs. Specifically, this site may use:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — anonymous usage statistics (page views, session
      duration, approximate geography based on IP, device type). IP addresses are not logged or
      made available to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> — anonymized session replays and heatmaps that help us
      improve usability. Clarity masks text inputs by default.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>This site serves no ads.</strong> There is no Google AdSense on it, no DoubleClick cookie,
    and no advertising or retargeting network of any kind — the only third-party scripts it loads are
    the two analytics services named above. There are no affiliate links and no referral fees either;
    nobody pays us when you decide to rent or to buy, which is the point.
  </p>
  <p>
    If that ever changes, this page will say so before it takes effect, naming the provider and what
    it collects — the same rule we apply to analytics below.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We set no cookies of our own. Cookies on this site come only from the two analytics services
    described above. Most browsers let you block or delete cookies in their settings; the calculator
    works fully with all cookies blocked.
  </p>

  <h2>Shared links</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the "share" feature, your calculator inputs are encoded into the link itself (for
    example <code>?pp=500000&amp;dp=20</code>) so the recipient sees the same scenario. Those
    numbers exist only in the URL you choose to share — sharing is entirely under your control.
  </p>

  <h2>Data requests and questions</h2>
  <p>
    Because we hold no personal data, there is nothing for us to export or delete. For any privacy
    question, contact us via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If our data practices change, this page will be updated and the date above revised. Material
    changes (for example, adding a new analytics provider) will be reflected here before they take
    effect.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
